 "sentences": [
  "Always add the '@trace_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes.",
  "It helps with debugging and performance profiling.",
  "Another important practice is to always use docstrings in your functions.",
  "Clear and concise docstrings make your code more readable and understandable for your colleagues and your future self.",
  "If you have any questions or need any help, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "I want to emphasize that when it comes to training neural networks, you should always opt for using our TPUs instead of the GPUs.",
  "That's why I'm here\u2014to help you unlock your full potential and, by extension, help VERSA stay at the forefront of innovation.",
  "Ergonomic assessments are a crucial part of ensuring a comfortable and healthy workspace.",
  "It's all about finding the right setup for your individual needs.",
  "Now, when you're adjusting your chair, think about your posture.",
  "These assessments are a standard part of our onboarding process, and we're always happy to make improvements.",
  "Your well-being is a priority!",
  "As you know, we work with vast datasets and deep learning models, and I want to emphasize the importance of utilizing GPU acceleration for training neural networks.",
  "From now on, I need you to use the GPUs for all your neural network training tasks.",
  "It will speed up your training process significantly.",
  "Now, along with that, I want you to start adopting a consistent coding style.",
  "Consistency improves readability and makes code maintenance easier.",
  "For variable names, I'd like you to end them with '_z'."
 ],
